"""Render human-facing module profiles and purpose routes from an editorial data source."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];out=root/'site/atlas';out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
baseline=json.loads((root/'migration/baseline/modules.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))['modules']
copy={
'qualiadb':('Keep knowledge in context.','A fact becomes more useful when we can ask where it came from, what it relates to and which circumstances matter. QualiaDB provides the knowledge and computational foundations used across this ecosystem.','Its graph, resource formats and computational libraries are designed to work together. The Lab lets you inspect actual query results rather than asking you to trust a feature list.','People need to question, correct and reuse information. Keeping its relationships and evidence available helps them make informed decisions.','graph.html',['vibescript','synth','qdnf']),
'webizen':('Put the person at the centre.','Webizen brings applications, knowledge and authorised capabilities into a human-facing computing environment. The aim is to help people act, create and cooperate with their own purposes and circumstances in view.','The application surface sits within a wider ecosystem of knowledge, hosts, instruments and creative tools. A choice about how to read information is kept separate from permission to access it.','A useful computer should support what a person is trying to do, including when they need assistance or a different form of presentation.','network_webizen.html',['webizen-host','aether','poet']),
'poet':('Turn an intention into a work.','Poet is the authoring application within the ecosystem. Its public material connects creative production with projects, knowledge and human-facing workflows.','It is an application surface over shared production and knowledge capabilities. The source inventory distinguishes implemented surfaces from specifications and future requirements.','Making something should not sever it from its meaning, sources or the people who will use it.','poet-app/index.html',['synth','vibescript','hypermedia']),
'vibescript':('Give the work a precise expression.','VibeScript describes authored work and the capabilities it requires. It is the language used by the production recipes you can inspect in this website.','A recipe names its host capabilities and can be evaluated into inspectable outputs. The same work can retain its source, resources and execution evidence.','A readable, reproducible account of how something was made gives creators and reviewers more agency.','vibe/index.html',['synth','etalon','qualiadb']),
'synth':('Make the work reproducible.','Synth produces media and other resources from Vibe recipes. The Lab uses the real producer to create native geometry, fields, pictures and sound.','Its production path packages outputs with source and runtime identity, content hashes and replay evidence. The artwork here includes those actual production records.','Creative work is easier to inspect, revisit and build upon when its origin and production process travel with it.','hypermedia-studio.html',['hypermedia','vibescript','etalon']),
'hypermedia':('Work across forms of expression.','Hypermedia production supplies operations for geometry, surfaces, images, typography, layout, motion, sound and other media. These operations are combined to make the works you see here.','The operations are shared capabilities invoked through recipes, rather than isolated effects copied into each demonstration. Native output can be inspected alongside the presentation.','People express and understand things through many forms. Shared production tools help those forms remain connected.','hypermedia-studio.html',['synth','etalon','anatomy']),
'etalon':('Bring computation into the experience.','Etalon supplies rendering, compute, signal and sensing providers used by the ecosystem. Its role becomes tangible when a native resource is rendered or a computation is executed.','The chosen execution path matters. The Lab records the actual provider and device conditions instead of treating every browser animation as proof of native computation.','Understanding what ran, and where, helps people judge whether a result is appropriate to their circumstances.','playground/etalon-vibe-harness.html',['anvil','qualiadb','synth']),
'anvil':('Understand the available machine.','Anvil concerns device capability and execution-routing information. That information helps other parts of the ecosystem choose an appropriate execution path.','Capability facts need to come from an actual probe. Unknown or unprobed hardware should remain unknown, rather than being reported as absent.','A visitor should get a useful experience on their own equipment, with an honest account of what it can run.','playground/etalon-vibe-harness.html',['etalon','aether','webizen-host']),
'aether':('Connect applications to their environment.','Aether provides application-framework and reactive interface foundations. Its role sits between application intent and the surfaces through which people interact.','It is part of the application and native-interface layer, while production, storage and rendering remain distinct responsibilities with explicit connections.','Consistent interaction and appropriate feedback help people move between tools without losing their place.','manuals/webizen-ui-architecture.md',['webizen','chora','etalon']),
'chora':('Give documents a place to live.','Chora concerns embedded web and spatial document experiences. It connects authored content to the environment in which it is read and used.','Document presentation is a component responsibility within the wider ecosystem. A spatial presentation should retain a readable, navigable counterpart.','Information should remain available when someone needs a different device, layout or way to navigate.','manuals/webizen-browser-operator.md',['aether','webizen','qualiadb']),
'webizen-host':('Make the conditions of participation clear.','Webizen Host concerns hosting, namespaces, deployment and stewardship. It is part of the machinery that makes an application or shared resource available under defined conditions.','A host is responsible for the capabilities it actually admits. A visitor preference or a client-side visual state must not be mistaken for host authority.','People need dependable boundaries as well as useful access: who may act, under which conditions, and with what recourse.','vibe-host-native-bridge.html',['webizen','web-civics','qdnf']),
'web-civics':('Make meaning and commitments inspectable.','Web Civics and the associated vocabulary work provide structured ways to express shared meaning and instruments used by the ecosystem.','The website demonstrates selected instrument behaviour with actual evaluation and clearly bounded examples. It does not equate a demonstration with general legal compliance.','Cooperation depends on understanding terms, responsibilities and available choices, not merely accepting an unexplained button.','agreement-instruments.html',['cooperation','qualiadb','webizen-host']),
'cooperation':('Support people doing things together.','Cooperation, Wellfare and work-graph concepts address care, participation and shared work. These are human purposes for the computing ecosystem, not an afterthought to its technical foundations.','Support needs, resources, responsibilities and relationships belong in the same account of an activity. The implementation plan includes positive assistance, correction and bounded delegation.','A human-centric ecosystem must help people participate, including when their needs differ or they need help to act.','agreement-ledger.html',['web-civics','webizen','qualiadb']),
'anatomy':('Understand life at different scales.','Anatomy contains authored spatial biological and welfare educational works. It connects structure, explanation and the production of inspectable assets.','Authored models, comparative scaffolds and qualified domain computations have different meanings. Their scope and evidence must stay visible when they are presented beautifully.','Seeing a living structure can make an explanation more accessible. Accuracy and appropriate educational framing remain essential.','playground/anatomy.html',['hypermedia','qualiadb','etalon']),
'ecopunk':('Keep the living world in the picture.','Ecopunk brings ecological and living-world themes into the ecosystem. Here, forests, water and landscape are subjects of inquiry and care as well as places to explore.','The natural world gives the experience its questions. A computational model and an artistic interpretation are identified separately from a measured observation.','Computing takes place within a biosphere and a society. Its usefulness should be considered in that wider context.','playground/living-world-showcase.html',['anatomy','qualiadb','cooperation']),
'qdnf':('Keep identity and connection coherent.','QDNF and identifier-fabric work concern the way entities, peers and network cells are identified and connected across the ecosystem.','The public documentation separates identifier concepts, peer runtime and network-cell behaviour. Those distinctions should survive a simplified explanation.','Stable references help people follow sources and retain context when information moves between places and representations.','qdnf.html',['webizen-host','qualiadb','webizen'])}
# The current inventory may use a more specific identifier for the identifier-fabric group.
for m in baseline:
 if m['id'] not in copy and 'qdnf' in (m['id']+' '+m['name']).lower():copy[m['id']]=copy['qdnf']
profiles=[]
for m in baseline:
 c=copy.get(m['id'])
 if not c:raise ValueError('Editorial profile required: '+m['id'])
 title,what,difference,why,source,related=c
 if not (Path('C:/github/qualiaDB/docs')/source).exists():source='index.html'
 profiles.append({**m,'headline':title,'what':what,'difference':difference,'why':why,'source_route':source,'related_modules':related,'locale':'en-AU','claim_state':'editorial explanation; availability must be checked against linked runtime evidence'})
content=root/'content/modules';content.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);(content/'profiles.en-AU.json').write_text(json.dumps({'schema':'webizen.editorial-profiles/v1','modules':profiles},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
esc=html.escape
cards=''.join(f'<a class="module-card" href="#{esc(m["id"])}"><span>{esc(m["name"])}</span><h3>{esc(m["headline"])}</h3><p>{esc(m["purpose"])}</p></a>' for m in profiles)
details=''.join(f'<article id="{esc(m["id"])}" class="module-detail"><div><p class="eyebrow">{esc(m["name"])}</p><h2>{esc(m["headline"])}</h2><p class="note">Source ownership: {esc(str(m.get("source_repository") or "being reconciled"))}</p></div><div><h3>What it does</h3><p>{esc(m["what"])}</p><h3>Its place in the ecosystem</h3><p>{esc(m["difference"])}</p><h3>Why it matters</h3><p>{esc(m["why"])}</p><p class="related">Connected with: {", ".join(esc(x) for x in m["related_modules"])}</p><a class="text-link" href="/source/{esc(m["source_route"])}">Inspect the source experience ↗</a> <a class="text-link" href="/lab/#collections">Find demonstrations and evidence ↗</a></div></article>' for m in profiles)
journeys=[('Everyday life','Start with a question that matters to you. Explore a place, try an instrument, and choose how much detail you want.','/'),('Making and developing','Inspect a Vibe recipe, produce an asset, query the graph and keep the resulting evidence.','/lab/#instruments'),('Research and learning','Follow the assumptions, methods and sources. Distinguish a model, an observation and a measured result.','/lab/#collections'),('Government and public service','Explore supported participation, accountable use of information and the conditions under which people can act.','#cooperation'),('Civil society and international cooperation','Consider agency, shared meaning, accessibility and different needs. Inspect the concrete examples and their limits.','#web-civics'),('Investment and stewardship','Examine what can be demonstrated today, how the modules depend on one another and what still needs qualification.','/lab/#recorded')]
journeyhtml=''.join(f'<a class="module-card" href="{url}"><h3>{esc(title)}</h3><p>{esc(body)}</p></a>' for title,body,url in journeys)
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en-AU"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Meet the components of the Webizen human-centric computing ecosystem: what they do, how they relate and why they matter."><title>The ecosystem — Webizen</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/lab/lab.css"><style>header{position:relative;background:#25493d}.atlas-title{background:#25493d;color:#f3edda;padding:70px 7%}.atlas-title p{max-width:700px;color:#c0cbb9}.module-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:25px}.module-card{padding:27px;background:#e2e6d9;text-decoration:none;border-top:1px solid #98aa98}.module-card span{font-size:11px;color:#886c3f}.module-card h3{font-size:29px;margin-top:18px}.module-card p{font-size:13px;color:#607366}.module-detail{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.35fr;gap:9%;padding:75px 0;border-top:1px solid #a5b5a0;scroll-margin-top:20px}.module-detail h3{font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.5px;margin:25px 0 12px}.module-detail p{color:#526d5c}.related{font-size:12px}@media(max-width:800px){.module-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.module-detail{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}}@media(max-width:500px){.module-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style><header><a class="brand" href="/">W<span>webizen<small>Human-centric computing</small></span></a><nav><a href="/">The living world</a><a href="/lab/">Infosphere Lab</a><a href="#purposes">Find your path</a></nav><span class="locale">English · AU</span></header><main><section class="atlas-title"><p class="eyebrow">People · purpose · possibility</p><h1>An ecosystem.<br>A shared human purpose.</h1><p>Knowledge, creative expression, computation and cooperation belong together. Meet the components, see how they connect, and discover what each makes possible.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="module-grid">'''+cards+'''</div></section><section class="section" id="purposes"><p class="eyebrow">Choose a starting question</p><h2>What brings you here?</h2><div class="module-grid">'''+journeyhtml+'''</div><p class="note">These are authored reading invitations. Choosing a purpose never grants authority or changes the evidence.</p></section><section class="section">'''+details+'''</section></main><footer><span>Webizen · A human-centric computing ecosystem</span><a href="/lab/">Enter the Infosphere Lab</a><a href="/">Return to the living world</a></footer></html>'''
(out/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');print('Rendered',len(profiles),'en-AU module profiles and six authored audience routes.')
